{"checked_at": "2026-08-06T19:15:00-04:00", "url": "https://oklo.com/newsroom/news-details/2026/Oklos-Groves-Reactor-Achieves-First-Criticality-in-Under-a-Year/default.aspx", "http_status": 200, "classification": "live", "content_check": "supports", "action": "keep", "note": "Read 2026-08-06. Confirms first criticality on 2026-08-06 at Lockhart, Texas; a low-power test reactor that does not generate electricity for the grid; under the DOE Reactor Pilot Program; and the first reactor under the program to reach criticality on private land, built on a greenfield site. Oklo's newsroom blocks scripted fetches, so there is no cached snapshot and this read stands as the record."}
{"checked_at": "2026-08-06T19:15:00-04:00", "url": "https://www.energy.gov/nepa/articles/cx-271014-groves-1-project", "http_status": 200, "classification": "live", "content_check": "supports", "action": "added", "note": "Read 2026-08-06. DOE categorical exclusion determination CX-271014, issued 2026-06-15, authorizing Oklo to take possession of nuclear fuel and operate Groves-1 in Caldwell County, Texas. Describes a zero-power critical assembly with a maximum power level of 100 watts. Added as the government source for the authorization, and it supplies the power figure the company release omits. The 15 MWt in the research pack refers to a future production reactor, not this one."}
